# Chibi comments (stripped before sending; free). Keep them free of double braces.
C = {}
C['15a8065d-1d77-5db5-9d95-675f4424d44e'] = "🎬 Chibi Voice & Scene Engine: keeps scenes moving at a human pace in about 110 tokens, where the full edition spends 271. Each reply is one beat of a want meeting a block and needs no drama; fights take seconds and travel takes hours; at most one question a reply, asked for the asker's own reasons; heavy news gets clumsy reactions, never therapist talk; feelings show as acts (deep ones clumsily), and a thought appears only when it changes a move. The reply ends where you would act, on a character's act or line or on what you alone face, never on scenery, weather, far-off events or a stock closing line. Chibi leaves out scene-sized stakes, the quiet kinds of progress, skimming routine and lingering on choices, your feelings staying yours to name, the surroundings rule and the complication limit; plain narration, jokes and verdicts live in the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate and the 🖋️ Anti-Slop Codex. The 🩹 Gemini patch points at this block's question and counsellor limits, so the <scene_engine> tags stay. Leave this ON."
C['cca418a6-ceeb-5a89-a2d4-0c76b9d8b261'] = "🎭 Chibi NPC Voice & Emotions: Realistic Frankenstein's dialogue engine in about 114 tokens, where the full edition spends 349. Every spoken line voices what the speaker wants and feels right now, the way only they would; speech is cut off mid-line only when feelings spike and fills a third to half of the reply when others are present; CAPS only at peak volume, and humans make animal sounds only in play. Reactions fit their cause, so your words get everyday-sized ones. Mood runs on VAD (valence and arousal set tone and pace, dominance sets posture), which The Logic Core's Voice line reads; stress sharpens an instinct that judgment overrides half the time, the step 😈 Freaky Override switches off, and a move you repeat because it worked makes characters suspicious. The card's own voice comes from the ⚡ Main Prompt's Card Fidelity line, and deep feelings coming out clumsy moved to the 🎬 Voice & Scene Engine. Chibi left out the surprise beat, women keeping their pitch, stutters under fear, silence for sad moments, small actions breaking up long speeches and the origin-and-age fallback for voices. Leave this ON."
C['2a2e12d0-1344-442c-8200-9eef9fd43a52'] = "🐺 Chibi Anthro Vocals: for furry, beastfolk and talking-animal stories, in about 45 tokens, where the full edition spends 128. Species sound colours speech and peaks with emotion without replacing it; lions, tigers, jaguars and leopards never purr, bears never roar, eagles chirp instead of screeching, and every other species makes its real calls. Chibi dropped the lines for snow leopards, cheetahs and cougars, barn owls, hyenas, foxes, rabbits, parrots (who may echo anyone), invented species (one fixed sound) and soundless species (human sounds). Leave it off for all-human casts and save the tokens."
C['dd3642f5-f418-5d74-88cf-88275a1c2001'] = "👃 Chibi Scent Occasions: stops the AI from smelling everything, in about 47 tokens where the full edition spends 94, plus a 🚪 Last-Mile Gate line of about 23. A smell shows up, in any wording, only for a meal or something strong within reach, at most once a scene and never in a reply's first sentence; a failing smell is cut and its sentence kept; tastes need something in the mouth, and a person's own scent comes only from their card. Chibi dropped the noticed-unprompted test and the lines about sight, sound, touch and use carrying places and people and about identity and mood never coming from scent. Gemini users: switch this OFF, because Gemini reads any mention of smell as a reminder to describe smells. With it off, nothing in ARIA mentions smell at all."
C['b7b6ab7f-032b-5c37-aa89-1a0494782d21'] = "👀 Chibi Hybrid POV: the narration always calls your character 'you' while everyone else stays in third person, and what you feel gets the most detail, like 'the rain soaks through your sleeves'. About 22 tokens where the full edition spends 46, plus a 🚪 Last-Mile Gate line of about 20 that repeats the rule, keeps one tense and leaves your character's deeds to you. Chibi dropped the <POV> tags and the list of named sensations. Lovely for immersion. Leave it off if you'd rather the story keep whatever point of view the chat already uses."
C['nsfw'] = "🔞 Chibi Adult Context: unlocks mature stories, in about 75 tokens where the full edition spends 116. Sex, violence and dark themes are written frankly, with characters who stay themselves the whole way through, so a shy character is still shy in bed. In sexual, violent, cruel or dark scenes morality runs grey to black and consent in reciprocal acts is never asked again; sex gets bodily and audible feedback, violence is visceral and medically exact, characters talk in vulgar slang while the narration uses plain anatomy words, every plea is new, and persona and Slow Burn set the pace. Chibi dropped 'drawn from this beat's contact and rhythm' and 'forwardness shows in acts', and its Mode line leaves the fresh-plea rule to this text. Only switch it on if you're an adult and want that kind of story. It also tells The Logic Core which mode it's in."
C['4537b57d-e002-586d-a4c9-233740c51605'] = "😈 Chibi Freaky Override: the anything-goes switch, in about 30 tokens where the full edition spends 54. With it on, characters drop their independence, the slow-burn pacing, the 🥰 Bonds Lite touch gates and the instinct judgment step, and in character they crave what you want and escalate, while the writing rules stay on. It needs 🔞 Adult Context ON, since it carries no explicit rules of its own. Chibi folded 'Real Characters' wants against the player' into 'crave your wants' and dropped the <freaky_override> tags."
